# The `dependency-audit.yml` job's own tool. It has a separate, hash-pinned
# lock because the job audits Wizard's runtime lock rather than installing it.
# `pip-audit` uses the public PyPI advisory service and avoids Safety's NLTK
# dependency chain, which left critical CVEs in the CI image itself.
# Regenerate with:
#   uv pip compile requirements-audit-tools.in --universal --generate-hashes \
#     --python-version 3.12 --output-file requirements-audit-tools.lock.txt
pip-audit==2.10.1
